Android Application Reverse Engineering Methodologies

Part 4 — React Native Application Reverse Engineering Methodology (Beginner → Expert)

> Goal: Learn how to systematically understand React Native applications. Unlike traditional Android applications, React Native executes most application logic in JavaScript (or TypeScript compiled to JavaScript) while delegating platform-specific operations to native Android components. By the end of this section, you should be able to reconstruct the JavaScript architecture, native integration, rendering pipeline, communication mechanisms, and runtime behavior of a React Native application.



> Core Principle:
React Native applications consist of two cooperating systems: the JavaScript application and the native Android host. Reverse engineer both, then reconstruct how they communicate.




