Stage 29 — Common React Native Investigation Mistakes

Avoid

Treating React Native as a traditional Android application.

Assuming the Android Java/Kotlin code contains most business logic.

Ignoring the JavaScript module graph.

Confusing reconciliation with business behavior.

Overlooking state management architecture.

Ignoring Native Modules, JSI, and bridge communication.

Assuming every component re-render indicates meaningful logic changes.



---

Stage 30 — React Native APK Methodology Master Checklist

By the end of this stage, you should be able to:

✅ Identify and profile React Native applications and their JavaScript engine.

✅ Reconstruct component hierarchies, navigation, state management, and rendering behavior.

✅ Understand the JavaScript runtime, module graph, reconciliation process, and asynchronous execution model.

✅ Trace communication between JavaScript and Android through Native Modules, JSI, TurboModules, and related interfaces.

✅ Distinguish handwritten application logic from framework infrastructure and generated code.

✅ Correlate static reconstruction with runtime behavior to validate execution and state changes.

✅ Produce comprehensive architectural documentation explaining both the JavaScript application and its interaction with the Android platform.



